## Review

Focused review of `src/application/task/task-access.ts` and all seven task use cases. **Verdict: project-scoped, owner-only authorization is implemented consistently across every CRUD path. No authorization bypass or missing check was found in the application layer.**

### Authorization model

Access is **project-owner only** (not assignee-based). That matches the ADR in `DECISIONS.md` and the integration tests.

| Use case | Helper | Check | Order |
|----------|--------|-------|-------|
| **create** | `requireOwnedProject` | `project.assertOwnedBy(userId)` | Before `save` |
| **list** | `requireOwnedProject` | same | Before `findByProjectId` |
| **get** | `requireTaskAccessibleByProjectOwner` | load task → load project → `task.assertAccessibleByProjectOwner` | Before return |
| **update** | `requireTaskAccessibleByProjectOwner` | same | Before `update` |
| **delete** | `requireTaskAccessibleByProjectOwner` | same | Before `delete` |
| **assign** | `requireTaskAccessibleByProjectOwner` | same | Before `update` |
| **changeStatus** | `requireTaskAccessibleByProjectOwner` | same | Before `update` |

Central helpers in `task-access.ts`:

```13:54:src/application/task/task-access.ts
export async function requireOwnedProject(
  projectRepository: ProjectRepository,
  projectId: ProjectId,
  userId: UserId,
): Promise<Project> {
  const project = await projectRepository.findById(projectId);

  if (project === null) {
    throw new ProjectNotFoundError();
  }

  project.assertOwnedBy(userId);

  return project;
}

